# Batter Up: sample environment.
#
# Nothing here is required. The demo needs no API key, no account and no network:
# it replays committed JSON under ui/data/. Every variable below is optional and has a working default.
#
# The scripts do not read a .env file. To use one of these, export it in your shell,
# for example:  PORT=9000 scripts/serve.sh

# Port for scripts/serve.sh (default 8765)
# PORT=8765

# Where scripts/setup.sh creates or finds the Python venv (default ~/hb-overnight/.venv)
# HB_VENV=~/hb-overnight/.venv

# Python interpreter for the build and test scripts (default: the venv's Python)
# PY=~/hb-overnight/.venv/bin/python

# Chrome binary for the browser smoke test (default: found automatically)
# CHROME=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome

# 1 also runs the slow full-evening engine tests
# HB_SLOW=1

# 1 skips the heavy-run lock (needed on Windows and Linux without lockf)
# HB_LOCK_HELD=1

# Parallel workers for the capacity planner build (default 1)
# PLAN_WORKERS=1
